= Concentrated liquidity — Technical =

Range-based liquidity can be represented as virtual reserves within interval [p_a,p_b]. As price traverses the interval, the position transforms between the two assets; outside the interval it becomes single-sided and contributes no active swap depth until price re-enters.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* concentrated liquidity ≠ Uniswap by identity
* capital efficiency ≠ guaranteed LP profitability
* out-of-range position ≠ vanished assets

